import json,statistics,math,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
p=Path('results/mnist_reconstruction_alignment_20261106');r=json.loads((p/'results.json').read_text());t=json.loads((p/'test_results.json').read_text());selected=json.loads((p/'selection.json').read_text());arms=['decoder_only','ranking','meta','ranking_meta']
lines=['# Reconstruction ranking and training-through-refinement','', '24 sequential-training runs: three seeds × two task orders × four decoder objectives. The proven sparse hybrid5 core is unchanged bitwise in EVERY run, checked against saved reference checkpoints. No historical data replay. Decoder adds31,280 trainable parameters. All inference updates change temporary per-image gates only; no labels, task identity, support set or stream context.','', '## Validation comparison','', '| Decoder objective | 0 updates | 1 update | 3 updates | 5 updates | Training s |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
summary=[]
for arm in arms:
 rr=[a for a in r if a['arm']==arm];cells=[]
 for step in [0,1,3,5]:
  v=[statistics.mean(a['validation'][str(step)]['accuracy']*100 for a in rr if a['seed']==s) for s in [101,102,103]];cells.append(f'{statistics.mean(v):.2f} ± {statistics.stdev(v):.2f}%');summary.append(dict(arm=arm,steps=step,validation=statistics.mean(v),seed_sd=statistics.stdev(v)))
 lines.append('| '+arm+' | '+' | '.join(cells)+f" | {statistics.mean(a['training_seconds'] for a in rr):.2f} |")
lines+=['',f"Overall validation choice: **{selected['overall']['arm']}, {selected['overall']['steps']} updates**. All zero-update configurations have identical core predictions; ties between names are not meaningful.",f"Best positive-update validation candidate: **{selected['positive']['arm']}, {selected['positive']['steps']} updates**.",'', '## Prespecified test curves for selected positive-update arm and decoder-only control','', '| Decoder objective | Updates | Test accuracy | Reconstruction error | Corrected | Newly wrong |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for arm in sorted(set(a['arm'] for a in t)):
 rr=[a for a in t if a['arm']==arm]
 for step in [0,1,3,5]:
  v=[statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['accuracy']*100 for a in rr if a['seed']==s) for s in [101,102,103]];recon=statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['reconstruction'] for a in rr);corrected=statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['corrected'] for a in rr);harmed=statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['harmed'] for a in rr);lines.append(f'| {arm} | {step} | {statistics.mean(v):.2f} ± {statistics.stdev(v):.2f}% | {recon:.4f} | {corrected:.1f} | {harmed:.1f} |')
lines+=['','Counts average six10,000-image evaluations. SD uses three seed means over orders. Candidate settings chosen by mean validation only; test curves show prespecified counts without selecting again. This remains an exploratory, repeatedly inspected MNIST benchmark.','', '## What was trained','', '- All arms retain the identical original hybrid5 classification/auxiliary objective. Decoder uses168→32 tanh→784 sigmoid. Ordinary reconstruction anchor uses trace-selected masked features; all branch features are detached for new decoder losses. Mask draws are matched across methods; sampled-route randomness uses a separate copied RNG state.','- Ranking samples four gate configurations: trace route, current magnitude-soft route, and25%/50% trace perturbations. Label-based full-image CE selects best and worst per image. Only pairs with a correct best prediction and CE gap>.1 qualify. Decoder penalty .5×max(0,.02+Rgood−Rbad), plus anchor reconstruction. No gradient through the discrete teacher selection.','- Meta objective differentiates through ONE reconstruction-driven gate update and adds .5 post-update classification CE, using true training labels but frozen/detached class features and readout. Thus classification feedback reaches the decoder through a second-order derivative, while core classifier weights stay on their baseline trajectory. Combined arm adds both penalties.','- Two30%-masked views/image; masked foreground-weighted pixel MSE, no input-to-decoder skips. Inference matches the training update: s←s−.1 grad/(per-image RMSgrad+1e-6). Later steps include .01 KL to initial gates. Each image starts independently.','', '## Interpretation limits','', 'This tests whether decoder-only objective alignment can improve an already trained classifier without harming its core features. It does not test end-to-end meta-updates into branch weights, separately learned class-conditional generators, broader temperature/weight grids or replay-protected decoders. The decoder still learns sequentially, so loss of its old-context verification ability remains possible. Training through one update need not generalize to longer trajectories. Lower reconstruction error or a training ranking margin alone is not proof of better semantic decisions.','', 'Two tests passed: outer classification gradients reach the decoder through the gate update, and all added objectives leave core gradients absent while preserving matched mask RNG draws. Every complete run also passed the bitwise core-checkpoint assertion.','', 'Pre-experiment progress record: ../../reports/progress_20261106/PROGRESS_AND_BEST_MODEL.md. Best-model checkpoint/source checksum manifest was written before this experiment.']
(p/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');(p/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
manifest=json.loads(Path('reports/progress_20261106/BEST_MODEL_MANIFEST.json').read_text());assert all(hashlib.sha256(Path(a['path']).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==a['sha256'] for a in manifest)
print('\n'.join(lines[:24]));print('Preserved baseline manifest verified.')
